# Generated fleet data. Half a million rows, regenerated in about seventy
# seconds by `cobalt generate`, and invalidated by a one-line config change.
# Carrying it in the repository would be tens of megabytes of derived files.
#
# The leading slash is load-bearing. Written as `data/` this pattern matches a
# directory called `data` at ANY depth, which silently excluded the whole of
# src/cobalt/data/ from the first commit. Everything still worked locally, and
# a fresh clone was missing a subpackage.
/data/

# Everything else under results/, analysis/ and artifacts/ IS committed: the
# README's tables are checked against results/default/summary.json on every
# push, so those files are load-bearing. Only the smoke run's output is not.
results/ci/
analysis/ci/
artifacts/ci/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
/build/
/dist/
.venv/
venv/

# Tooling
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
.mypy_cache/

# Editors and operating systems
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
